<!-- ============ CHAPTER 1 :: COVID ============ -->
<section class="chapter" id="ch1">
  <div class="ch-inner reveal">
    <span class="ch-tag red">// CHAPTER ONE</span>
    <div class="ch-num">01</div>
    <h1 class="ch-title">THE PLAGUE YEARS</h1>
    <p class="ch-meme">a.k.a. that time the whole world hit pause</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">The 2020s opened with the world already holding its breath. By early 2020, a new sickness called <span class="vocab" data-term="covid19">COVID-19</span> had stopped being a faraway news story and become a global emergency. Schools closed. Offices emptied. Hospitals filled up. People started wearing masks everywhere.</p>

      <p>Words you had never thought about before became part of normal life. <span class="vocab" data-term="quarantine">Quarantine</span>. <span class="vocab" data-term="lockdown">Lockdown</span>. Social distancing. Case counts. Six feet apart. Wash your hands for twenty seconds. Sing happy birthday twice.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="covid_virus" alt="Microscope view of the coronavirus showing its spiky crown-like surface in purple and blue.">
      <div class="caption">// the actual virus, up close. those spikes are how it grabs onto your cells. that crown of spikes is also why it's called a coronavirus, since "corona" means crown.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>The pandemic did not hit everyone the same. Older people, people with certain health problems, frontline workers, people without much money, and many people in racial and ethnic minority groups got sicker more often. They also had jobs they could not do from home. They lived in crowded housing. They had less access to doctors. <span class="vocab" data-term="pandemic">A pandemic</span> sounds like a single event, but it really showed how unequal life already was.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <div class="sensitive-wrap" data-sensitive>
        <div class="sensitive-cover">
          <span class="warning">⚠ HEAVY IMAGE</span>
          <div>Aerial view of a Brazilian cemetery during the pandemic, showing many freshly dug graves.</div>
          <small>tap anywhere to reveal</small>
        </div>
        <img src="" data-img="mass_graves" alt="Aerial view of rows of freshly dug graves at a Brazilian cemetery during the COVID-19 pandemic.">
      </div>
      <div class="caption">// Manaus, Brazil, 2020. workers digging graves around the clock. moments like this are why the pandemic felt different from anything most people had lived through.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="meme-callout">
      "THE WORLD SHRANK<br>TO THE SIZE OF A SCREEN."
      <small>// AND WE NEVER REALLY UN-SHRANK</small>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Then came the science fix. The <span class="vocab" data-term="mrna">mRNA vaccines</span> rolled out faster than anyone thought possible. The Pfizer-BioNTech and Moderna shots gave your cells a temporary instruction sheet to build a tiny harmless piece of the virus. Your immune system practiced on that piece, then knew what to attack if the real thing showed up. They did not give you COVID. They taught your body what COVID looks like.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="first_vaccine" alt="An older woman in a Christmas sweater receives one of the first COVID-19 vaccines from a nurse.">
      <div class="caption">// Margaret Keenan, age 90, becomes the first person in the world to get a tested COVID vaccine outside of a trial. December 8, 2020, United Kingdom.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="vibe-box yellow">
      <h4>VIBE CHECK :: lockdown moment</h4>
      <p>Suddenly everyone was baking sourdough bread. People learned the entire Renegade dance on TikTok. Tiger King ate the entire month of April 2020. Animal Crossing turned into a virtual hangout spot. Zoom backgrounds became personality. We were all in our houses, but somehow online together more than ever.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="social_distance_circles" alt="Aerial view of a park with white circles painted on the grass to keep people six feet apart.">
      <div class="caption">// Dolores Park, San Francisco. parks painted big white circles on the grass so people could hang out outside but stay six feet apart. one of the most 2020 pictures ever taken.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p><span class="vocab" data-term="remote_work">Remote work</span>, online school, Zoom-style video calls, QR-code menus, DoorDash dinners, telehealth doctor visits. Some of it was great. Many people loved skipping the commute. But the costs were real. Students fell behind. People felt isolated and lonely. The lines between work, school, and home turned into blurry mush. The pandemic made the home into office, classroom, theater, restaurant, church, clinic, and bunker, all at once.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="empty_times_square" alt="Times Square in New York City completely empty during the COVID-19 lockdown.">
      <div class="caption">// Times Square at noon. usually packed shoulder to shoulder. in spring 2020 it looked like a movie set after the credits rolled.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <div class="sensitive-wrap" data-sensitive>
        <div class="sensitive-cover">
          <span class="warning">⚠ EMOTIONAL CONTENT</span>
          <div>A memorial wall with red hearts for people who died of COVID, plus photos pinned up by their families.</div>
          <small>tap anywhere to reveal</small>
        </div>
        <img src="" data-img="memorial_wall" alt="A person adds a name to the COVID-19 Memorial Wall in London, which is covered in thousands of red painted hearts.">
      </div>
      <div class="caption">// the National COVID Memorial Wall, London. every red heart is one person who died of COVID in the UK. families painted them and added names so the dead would not just be a number.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="reflect">
      <h4>REFLECT</h4>
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">Take a beat. Think about these:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>What is one thing that changed about your school or family during the pandemic that is still different now?</li>
        <li>The text says the pandemic made some problems worse for some groups of people. Why might a job, a house, or who your doctor is make a virus more dangerous?</li>
      </ol>
      <textarea placeholder="jot a thought here if you want. nothing gets saved, this is just for u..."></textarea>
