<!-- ============ CHAPTER 5 :: CULTURE, AI, TRUMP 2.0 ============ -->
<section class="chapter" id="ch5">
  <div class="ch-inner reveal">
    <span class="ch-tag red">// CHAPTER FIVE</span>
    <div class="ch-num">05</div>
    <h1 class="ch-title">PHONES, AI, &amp; THE SECOND TRUMP ERA</h1>
    <p class="ch-meme">our entire culture, but make it scrollable</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">The cultural life of the 2020s runs through your smartphone. TikTok. Instagram Reels. YouTube Shorts. Streaming. Group chats. Influencers. Discord servers. Live-streamed Fortnite tournaments. The vibes are nonstop, fast, and personalized.</p>

      <p>Behind almost all of it is an <span class="vocab" data-term="algorithm">algorithm</span>. An algorithm is a set of step-by-step rules a computer follows. It's basically a recipe for a machine. Your "For You" feed isn't random. The algorithm predicts what you'll watch, like, share, or argue with, then serves you more of that.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="algorithm_diagram" alt="A simple diagram showing input going into a green diamond labeled algorithm, which produces output.">
      <div class="caption">// the basic shape of an algorithm. input goes in, the rules do their thing, output comes out. when your input is "things i watched all the way through" the output is "more of that, but tuned tighter."</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>That makes your phone feel kind of psychic. It also means the platforms have huge power over what people pay attention to. The same algorithm that knows you love cat videos can also push you toward outrage or misinformation if that's what keeps you scrolling longer.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="vibe-box pink">
      <h4>VIBE CHECK :: the 2020s pop culture all-stars</h4>
      <p>Taylor Swift went on a tour so big it moved local economies. Beyoncé released RENAISSANCE and the Cowboy Carter era. Bad Bunny made Spanish-language pop the biggest sound on Earth. K-pop fans organized like an army online. Marvel hit ceiling-shattering highs and brutal lows. Stranger Things, Squid Game, Wednesday, and The Bear made streaming the new water cooler. Wordle and Connections turned word games into a whole morning ritual. Among Us made "sus" a feeling. Anyone said "no thoughts, head empty" out loud yet?</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Then, on <strong>November 30, 2022</strong>, the world changed again. OpenAI released <strong>ChatGPT</strong>. It was free. It was easy to use. You could just type a question and it would answer in normal sentences. Within five days it had a million users. Within two months, a hundred million.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="chatgpt" alt="A phone showing the ChatGPT logo, with the OpenAI logo on a screen in the background.">
      <div class="caption">// ChatGPT, the chatbot that lit the AI fuse. before this, "AI" was a buzzword. after this, your grandma had used it.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>What is ChatGPT? It is a <span class="vocab" data-term="generative_ai">generative AI</span>, which is a kind of artificial intelligence that creates new stuff (words, pictures, code, sound) based on patterns it learned from huge piles of human-made data. Underneath the friendly interface is something called a <span class="vocab" data-term="neural_network">neural network</span>, layers of math designed to copy the rough shape of how brain cells connect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <img src="" data-img="neural_network" alt="A diagram showing a neural network with input, hidden, and output layers of connected circles.">
      <div class="caption">// a neural network in cartoon form. data goes in the left, gets passed through layers of math, and a prediction comes out the right.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Generative AI moved into school, work, art, customer service, search, and yes, into cheating on homework. It made writing faster. It made fake media easier. It changed conversations about jobs, copyright, school rules, and what counts as "your" work. By 2024 and 2025, AI was inside everything. Photo apps. Search engines. Grandma's text messages. The phone you're reading this on probably has an AI button.</p>

      <p>Other 2020s tech that shaped daily life: electric cars (Tesla, then everyone), smart homes (Alexa, Google Home), delivery apps (DoorDash, Uber Eats), endless monthly subscriptions, wearables that track your heart and your steps, and voice assistants that listen way more than they tell you. Convenience went up. So did surveillance, distraction, fees, and dependence on platforms.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="meme-callout" style="border-left-color: var(--yellow); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 var(--yellow);">
      "MORE CONNECTED. MORE WATCHED.<br>MORE ENTERTAINED. MORE DISTRUSTFUL."
      <small>// THE 2020s IN ONE LINE</small>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>In 2024, <strong>Donald Trump was elected president again</strong>. He defeated Vice President Kamala Harris, who was the candidate after Joe Biden withdrew from the race. Trump won the national vote with 50.7% to Harris's 48.5%. His comeback showed that January 6, the criminal investigations, inflation, immigration fights, and distrust of institutions had not ended Trump's political movement. If anything, those things became part of his pitch.</p>

      <p>Earlier that year, in July 2024, Trump survived an assassination attempt at a rally in Butler, Pennsylvania. A gunman fired from a nearby rooftop. A bullet grazed Trump's ear. One rally attendee was killed. Two more were wounded. The photo of Trump standing up afterward with his fist raised became one of the most famous American images of the decade.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="image-card">
      <div class="sensitive-wrap" data-sensitive>
        <div class="sensitive-cover">
          <span class="warning">⚠ INTENSE IMAGE</span>
          <div>Donald Trump with blood on his ear, fist raised in front of an American flag, surrounded by Secret Service agents after the assassination attempt.</div>
          <small>tap anywhere to reveal</small>
        </div>
        <img src="" data-img="trump_rally" alt="Donald Trump with his fist raised, blood on his ear, surrounded by Secret Service agents, with an American flag behind him after the July 2024 assassination attempt.">
      </div>
      <div class="caption">// Butler, Pennsylvania, July 13, 2024. seconds after a bullet grazed his ear. the image went around the world in minutes.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>So what does the 2020s look like, so far? A decade of compression. Pandemic and protest and election denial and war and inflation and Roe and AI and streaming and fandom and migration and climate anxiety and great-power rivalry, all delivered through the same glowing rectangle in your pocket. The decade is not over. Its full meaning is still being decided. But its central conflict is already pretty clear ::</p>
    </div>

    <div class="meme-callout">
      "EVERYBODY IS ONLINE.<br>NOBODY AGREES ON WHAT IS REAL."
      <small>// LITERALLY THE DEFINING TENSION OF THE DECADE</small>
    </div>

    <div class="reflect">
      <h4>REFLECT</h4>
